From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: alesx2io <96351978+alesx2io@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 12:50:24 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] dash: parts: Give the touch host processing its edge filter
 and orientation

On HyperOS the framework sends the display rotation to the touchfeature
service (mode 8) on every rotation, and a mode reset leaves the edge
filter (mode 7) at the panel default. Nothing does either here, so the
service runs with the edge filter off and fingers resting on the edges
register as taps (random taps in the camera).

Set the edge filter to its default and keep the panel orientation in
sync with the display rotation from Parts, again if the service
restarts. Declare the service types in the public policy so the
system_ext app can reach it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
